    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="9.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Af">Af</ref> 9.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="9.1" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="54" ed="#liebermann"/>Á sie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="36" target="#Af_9-1.lnote.oe.36"/> þæt wite LX<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="40" target="#Af_9-1.lnote.oe.40"/> scill’, oð ðæt angylde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="41" target="#Af_9-1.lnote.oe.41"/> árise to XXX<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="42" target="#Af_9-1.lnote.oe.42"/> scill’<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="43" target="#Af_9-1.lnote.oe.43"/>; siððan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="44" target="#Af_9-1.lnote.oe.44"/> hit to ðam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="45" target="#Af_9-1.lnote.oe.45"/> árise þæt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="46" target="#Af_9-1.lnote.oe.46"/> angylde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="47" target="#Af_9-1.lnote.oe.47"/>, siððan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="44" target="#Af_9-1.lnote.oe.44"/> sie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="36" target="#Af_9-1.lnote.oe.36"/> þæt wite CXX<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="48" target="#Af_9-1.lnote.oe.48"/> scill’.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="9.1" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="54" ed="#liebermann"/>A sy ðæt wite LX scill', oð ðæt angylde arise to XXX scill'; siððan hit to ðæm arise ðæt angylde, siððan sy<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_9-1.lnote.oe.3"/> þæt wite CXX scill'.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="9.1" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="55" ed="#liebermann"/>A sy þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> wíte syxti scill', oþ þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> angylde arise to ðrittig scill'; syððan hit to ðæm aríse þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> angylde, syþþan sy þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> wite hundtwelftig.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="9.1" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="55" ed="#liebermann"/>Sit semper<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Af_9-1.lnote.oe.6"/> wita LX solid., donec angildum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#Af_9-1.lnote.oe.16"/> exurgat ad triginta sol.; postquam angildum ad id surgit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#Af_9-1.lnote.oe.17"/> (crescit), postea sit wita centum uiginti solidi.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="68" ed="#attenborough"/>Á sie þæt wite LX scill', oð ðæt angylde árise to XXX scill'; siððan hit to ðam árise þæt angylde, siððan sie þæt wite CXX scill'.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="11" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="304" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Á sie þæt wite LX scill, oððæt angylde árise to XXX scill; siððan hit to ðam árise þæt angylde, siððan sie þæt wite CXX scill.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="55" ed="#liebermann"/>Das Strafgeld betrage jedesmal<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_9-1.lnote.de.1"/> 60 Schill.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_9-1.lnote.de.2"/>, bis das einfache Ersatzgeld<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_9-1.lnote.de.3"/> auf 30 Schill. steigt; sobald es dazu steigt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_9-1.lnote.de.4"/> das Ersatzgeld, von da ab betrage das Strafgeld 120 Schill.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_9-1.lnote.de.5"/></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">Let the fine always be 60 shillings, until the single compensation rises to 30 shillings; as soon as the compensation rises to that, from then on let the fine be 120 shillings.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="69" ed="#attenborough"/>Until the value<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Af_9-1.attnote.n.1"/> amounts to 30 shillings, the fine shall be 60 shillings in every case. When the [said] value amounts to this sum, the fine shall be 120 shillings.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="412" ed="#whitelock"/>The fine is always to be 60 shillings until the simple compensation rises to 30 shillings; when the simple compensation has risen to that, the fine is afterwards to be 120 shillings.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="305" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>The fine shall always be 60 shillings until the single-recompense reaches 30 shillings; after the single-recompense reaches this amount or higher, then the fine shall be 120 shillings.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="272"><label>cross-reference</label> <ref target="clause:Af_6">Af 6</ref> <quote>6, (ref. 9:1)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="307"><label>cf.</label> <ref target="clause:Af_11">Af 11</ref> <quote>Carole Hough, adducing §29 (in which a man who rapes a female slave must pay 5 shillings restitution plus the 60 shilling fine required by §11)</quote></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_9-1.lnote.oe.36" n="36" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">54</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sy <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sy Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_9-1.lnote.oe.40" n="40" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">54</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sixtig <hi rend="italic">So;</hi> syxtig <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sixtig So; syxtig Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_9-1.lnote.oe.41" n="41" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">54</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so;</hi> -ld <hi rend="italic">So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic; -ld So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_9-1.lnote.oe.42" n="42" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">54</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">þrittigum <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">þrittigum So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_9-1.lnote.oe.43" n="43" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">54</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">scyll.' <hi rend="italic">So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">scyll.' So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_9-1.lnote.oe.44" n="44" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">54</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Syþþan <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Syþþan Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_9-1.lnote.oe.45" n="45" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">54</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">þæm <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">þæm Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_9-1.lnote.oe.46" n="46" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">54</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">þ. a. si. <hi rend="italic">fehlt So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">þ. a. si. lacking in So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_9-1.lnote.oe.47" n="47" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">54</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so;</hi> -ld <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic; -ld Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_9-1.lnote.oe.48" n="48" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">54</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">hundtwelftig <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">hundtwelftig So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_9-1.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">54</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">y <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">y on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_9-1.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">55</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_9-1.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">55</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-de <hi rend="italic">K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-de K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_9-1.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">55</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">nur</hi> su. <hi rend="italic">Lond; nur</hi> cre. <hi rend="italic">übrige</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">only su. Lond; only cre. the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_9-1.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">53</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">= in jedem Fall, regelmässig</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">= in every case, regularly</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_9-1.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">53</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Strafgeldfixum 12. 13</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Strafgeldfixum 12. 13</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_9-1.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">53</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">angilde</hi> (<hi rend="italic">s. Wb</hi>) betrachtet Toller <hi rend="italic">Suppl.</hi> als normalen no. und ac. In So Ld fehlt zwar je einmal <hi rend="italic">-e,</hi> aber sie lassen öfter die Endung fort</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Toller <hi rend="italic">Suppl.</hi> regards <hi rend="italic">angilde</hi> (<hi rend="italic">see Wb</hi>) as the normal nom. and acc. It is true that So and Ld each lack the <hi rend="italic">-e</hi> once, but they often omit the ending</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_9-1.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">53</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Optativ, weil im übergeordneten Satz Opt. der Aufforderung steht; Wülfing <hi rend="italic">Syntax</hi> II 110. — In Q lautet Lond wörtlicher, also früher</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Optative, because the superordinate clause has an optative of exhortation; Wülfing <hi rend="italic">Syntax</hi> II 110. — In Q, Lond reads more literally, and is therefore earlier</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_9-1.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">53</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. o.</hi> 6³</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. above</hi> 6³</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_9-1.lnote.de.0" n="0" source="#liebermann-erkl" rend="wholeClause"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">53</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Vor 9, 1 sollte neues Kapitel beginnen. —</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">A new chapter should begin before 9, 1. —</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Af_9-1.attnote.n.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">195</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">i.e.</hi> the value of the article stolen, or the damages incurred for an offence. Note the complete change of subject.</seg></note>
      </div>
